1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Network changes rarely fail in isolation.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
A maintenance outage, new traffic, or a capacity constraint
can create failures somewhere completely unexpected.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,733
InfraTwin lets an engineer model those changes
before they reach production.

4
00:00:15,733 --> 00:00:20,700
The key is WebMCP. Instead of sending an agent
a stale API copy,

5
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:25,733
InfraTwin lets the engineer and agent operate on the same live,
unsaved Network and ChangePlan in the browser.

6
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:33,000
The engineer takes a Northeast-to-Central backbone link offline.
The agent reads that exact selection through WebMCP

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:42,367
and adds the expected twenty-percent Payments growth
to the same plan.

8
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:47,200
InfraTwin then runs deterministic routing
and capacity analysis.

9
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:53,233
The combined change overloads a different Southeast-to-Central corridor,
with the failure and utilization evidence linked back to the workspace.

10
00:00:53,233 --> 00:00:59,233
The agent does not invent that conclusion.
The evidence comes from machine-checkable computation.

11
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:06,233
That matters because real engineering includes constraints
an optimizer only learns when the human supplies them.

12
00:01:06,233 --> 00:01:12,800
The first mitigation is the cheapest capacity upgrade.
But the engineer knows that corridor cannot be modified,

13
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:20,200
so they lock it in the workspace.
The old proposal becomes stale immediately.

14
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:28,000
The agent observes the new restriction and asks InfraTwin
for another bounded design,

15
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,000
allowing routing and capacity changes around the protected resource.
After profiling the design engine,

16
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,000
candidate-path generation on the flagship workload fell
from 4.73 seconds to 0.51—roughly 9.35 times faster,

17
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,233
without changing the mathematical result.

18
00:01:45,233 --> 00:01:51,000
InfraTwin compares bounded alternatives by cost,
peak utilization, and verification status.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:59,300
The engineer remains in control of the choice,
and the selected design is reconstructed and independently verified before approval.

20
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:05,000
This is not limited to a tiny demo topology.
The browser workspace has also been validated

21
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,800
on a five-hundred-node, twelve-hundred-link,
four-hundred-demand network.

22
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:17,500
The integration uses native document.modelContext capability registration
and execution in the browser, not a parallel backend state.

23
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:25,000
Humans provide intent, operational knowledge, and approval.
Agents explore and revise alternatives.

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:35,200
InfraTwin supplies the deterministic evidence connecting the two,
so teams can falsify bad changes before production instead of discovering them afterward.
